r Protocol & Component Isolation** (`.ki-base/decisions/0002-render-protocol.md`, score: 6.315)\n   > # ADR-0002: Render Protocol & Component Isolation - **Status:** Accepted - **Date:** 2026-11-08 - **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers ## Context Rich supports...\n3. [KI] **ADR-0002: Render Protocol & Component Isolation** (`.ki-base/decisions/0002-render-protocol.md`, score: 6.315)\n   > # ADR-0002: Render Protocol & Component Isolation - **Status:** Accepted - **Date:** 2026-11-08 - **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers ## Context Rich supports...\n4. [KI] **KI: Rich Core (Console, Alignment & Core Layouts)** (`.ki-base/knowledge/KI_rich_align.md`, score: 5.229)\n   > ...constants, and alignment/column containers. It coordinates measurement, rendering, and terminal stream emission. ## Entry Points & Public API - `Console`: Primary interface orchestrating rendering, style resolution,...\n5. [KI] **_OVERVIEW — Project Overview** (`.ki-base/knowledge/_OVERVIEW.ki.md`, score: 4.784)\n   > ...2026-11-08 ## Overview Rich is a Python library for rendering rich text, tables, syntax highlighting, markdown, progress bars, and formatted data to terminal output and HTML. It serves as the primary rendering...\n\n*Showing 5 of 19 results. Call `ki_search(query='render protocol measurement embeddable component StyleType Text Panel Table', page=2)` (or `offset=5`) to view more.*"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_search"},"isError":false,"durationMs":131,"timestamp":1794170340442},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_fhKmTkbQpLuEAr6GbYYe52MI","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_instructions","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Global AI Instructions for ki-manager\n\n## 1. Project Navigation & Architecture\n`.ki-base` (knowledge_root) is the **system container** for the entire knowledge infrastructure (analogous to `.git/` in Git).\n\n```\n<project_root>/\n├── .ki-base/                 ← SYSTEM CONTAINER (do not pollute with .ki.md)\n│   ├── config.json             ← Machine-specific environment config (venv path, etc.)\n│   ├── ki_config.json          ← Project knowledge configuration\n│   ├── doc_config.json         ← Manifest of tracked modules and Knowledge Items\n│   ├── DIR_INDEX.md            ← Auto-generated project directory tree\n│   ├── coverage_matrix.md      ← Audit report (from audit_coverage)\n│   ├── knowledge/              ← STRICTLY ALL Knowledge Items (*.ki.md) live HERE!\n│   │   ├── _OVERVIEW.ki.md     ← Project overview stub (MUST NOT be deleted)\n│   │   └── <module>.ki.md      ← Module Knowledge Items\n│   └── decisions/              ← Architectural Decision Records (*.md ADRs)\n├── AGENTS.md                   ← Project instructions for AI agents in harness\n└── CLAUDE.md                   ← Instructions for Claude Code / Anthropic\n```\n\n- **`DIR_INDEX.md`** (`.ki-base/DIR_INDEX.md`) — project directory tree.\n- **`doc_config.json`** (`.ki-base/doc_config.json`) — manifest of tracked artifacts.\n- **`_OVERVIEW.ki.md`** (`.ki-base/knowledge/_OVERVIEW.ki.md`) — start here for high-level architecture.\n- **Harness & Agent Instructions Guide**: see `ki://agent-rules.md` or `ki_instructions(document=\"agent-rules\")` for recommended snippets for `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`.\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> 1. NEVER place `*.ki.md` files directly in the root of `.ki-base/`. All Knowledge Items must reside in `.ki-base/knowledge/`.\n> 2. NEVER delete `.ki-base/knowledge/`. The initial `_OVERVIEW.ki.md` (~640 bytes) is a bootstrap stub, not a duplicate. Deleting `knowledge/` breaks audit, scaffolding, and dependency analysis.\n\n## 2. Forced Efficiency (Anti-Hallucinations)\n1. **Mandatory Planning Template**:\n   Before making code changes, your initial plan (Implementation Plan) **MUST** include:\n   - **Affected layers**: [which subsystems are affected]\n   - **Read KIs**: [LIST of files from `.ki-base/knowledge/` which you read for this task]. *If the list is empty — read KIs before writing code!*\n   - **KIs Constraints**: [which approaches are prohibited by current architecture]\n\n2. **Strict Adherence**:\n   - Always read relevant KIs before modifying a module.\n- Use `ki_list()` to view all documented items, `ki_search(query=\"...\")` to find topics, and `ki_read(rel_path=\"...\")` to read documentation.\n   - For read-only analysis tools (`audit_coverage`, `generate_dir_index`, `ki_scaffold_status`, `git_diff_secured`), call `ki_call(tool=\"...\")`.\n   - For state-modifying operations (`git_checkpoint`, `write_know_file`, `edit_know_file`, `ki_scaffold`, `create_adr`), call `ki_mutate(tool=\"...\", args={...})`.\n   - To inspect schemas of available tools, call `ki_tools(name=\"<tool_name>\")`.\n   \n## 3. Workflow-driven Execution\n1. Check `ki://workflows/` resources or MCP Prompts if the user asks for a complex documentation task.\n2. These workflows are your \"operating system\". You **MUST** follow their steps exactly as written.\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_instructions"},"isError":false,"durationMs":134,"timestamp":1794170340446},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.encrypted\",\"data\":\"gAAAAABq8N3mlIPD5wdLeOOrWv-s4u7_eWxAYw63uFveP8XGMIYFFkmdBxf71WJ6WsMnPLSU-inCu3cPRbc3bE101NGBN1yKgKadLmSh0gvMyMU4wPZC25Xpk9xpqdfe6TPii5wJIXyLjZccBcvndFk1X-DVAbwSru_ntIuprsyE8CbQzXlloQjcVg8lRo0WleuotyK2l2rbbg7fcFX-2Dv88r3Eve_wiLafFO0-m-fDit0vB32TeXHjp8uJ9tk2JNIwb8tYk8aTAnVY_SidhOdrc0oGHcrz2kNP-onr70iXATxUbBLrhOWxGs1JjMhevg0ebeRgOyQRpJft49JroO674S7ZcvkceHLBMyn1kjCr22RkCk1j5uMZk3SwmgY14HQoP4Lrr74upchqyJwBLtOGRyW8fcbe7EioQBSozyuIo6DfaB9QDESashIBh7D7qBkgb3B8ad4CkdFHfu9VNE3OyynWseAFSR-I_9h5iqy6iVrM3RONXqLSfheFmS-pEr8bfgEDWoZ_K_N8QwNVJDZ2iz9_uWlXQ6o3ZLVb9ecIODcAeWY8a3R7FMnVVK5XnHo55PIrIgkS3aSfKYfkGiyRzjz4i71zeMbQlfUOZeaFJNMdm0wbdmIVgxPPsaQCoBP--6cPiZ0kpx2qZh88o-7aGPm_buoznyY-2tgwgnsMbXRyJK2l6RdD2O6DVrLHwGLWZ-9CAa38Zdo_0QU6gXKC3XR_FwOuzb4H0xCME-IOMn-9BsTtmYZN1Tel6EutTk7ACsVadaCBtT8PJWSzMT