.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"openai/gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":3,"output":175,"cacheRead":5033,"cacheWrite":1502,"reasoning":11,"totalTokens":6713,"cost":{"input":6.000000000000001e-7,"output":0.00020999999999999998,"cacheRead":0.00010066,"cacheWrite":0.0003755,"total":0.00068676,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794170340466,"responseId":"gen-1794170340-k4n7ImuXAlymmHzTsaWI","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":2798,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_uaOOJY5F7TtYJQbdX6RJ5gHH","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0002: Render Protocol & Component Isolation\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nRich supports arbitrary nested UI components (such as Panels inside Tables inside Trees). If custom components were allowed to mutate shared rendering options or directly manipulate the `Console` buffer, rendering would become non-deterministic, thread-unsafe, and incompatible with real-time displays like `Live` and `Progress`.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Mandatory Console Protocol:**  \n   All visual components must implement the public generator protocol:\n   ```python\n   def __rich_console__(self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\") -> \"RenderResult\":\n       ...\n       yield Segment(...)\n   ```\n   A component may optionally implement `__rich_measure__(self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\") -> Measurement` for dynamic sizing.\n\n2. **Strict Component Isolation Invariants:**\n   - **No Buffer Access:** Components must NEVER access or write to `console._buffer` or `console.file` directly. All output must be returned via `yield` as an iterable of `Segment` or renderable objects.\n   - **Options Immutability:** The passed `options: ConsoleOptions` instance is strictly read-only. Components must never mutate its fields. To adjust constraints for child components, use `options.update(...)` which returns a fresh copy.\n   - **Stateless Yielding:** Generators must be re-entrant and idempotent so that multiple render passes (e.g. measuring then rendering) produce identical results without side effects.\n\n3. **Internal Spacing Convention for Inline Badges:**\n   - In accordance with repository design conventions, inline badge components must enclose their inner text with exactly one space of padding inside the boundary caps: `\"( \"` + content + `\" )\"` for pill badges, and `\"[\" + \" \"` + content + `\" ]\"` for square badges.\n   - Example: `Badge(\"DEPLOYED\", pill=True, icon=\"★\")` must yield segments rendering as `\"( ★ DEPLOYED )\"`. Square badges render as `\"[ SYSTEM ALERT ]\"`. Measurement must include the 4 cells occupied by borders and inner spaces.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Components can be composed arbitrarily without side effects.\n- Direct console buffer writes or mutating shared options is treated as an architectural violation and rejected in code review.\n- Ensures seamless integration with `Live` displays and virtual screen buffers.\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":43,"timestamp":1794170343341},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_hU3LldJjFNrxuskTaFxVvS54","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Section 'Render Protocol' not found in '.ki-base/knowledge/KI_rich_markdown.md'."}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":51,"timestamp":1794170343345},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_Nlg6CfYyRjJ3aCOe6OMQ0Qp0","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# KI: Rich Core (Syntax, Tables, Text & Tracebacks)\n\n## Overview\nImplements high-level data presentation components: `Table` (grid formatting with auto-wrapping), `Text` (styled character spans), `Syntax` (Pygments code highlighting), `Traceback` (rich exception rendering), and `Tree` (hierarchical tree visualizations).\n\n## Entry Points & Public API\n- `Table`: Flexible 2D data grid with borders, column wrapping, and header styling.\n- `Text`: Rich text container applying styles to string slices without markup overhead.\n- `Syntax`: Code syntax highlighter powered by Pygments themes with line numbers.\n- `Traceback`: Formatted exception hook and renderable for stack traces with syntax context.\n- `Tree`: Hierarchical outline/tree view with custom branch guides and leaf nodes.\n- `Theme`: Named style mapping defining cohesive terminal color palettes.\n\n## Key Components\n| Class / Function | File | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Table` | `rich/table.py` | Grid container managing column widths, padding, vertical alignment, and borders |\n| `Text` | `rich/text.py` | Span-based styled text representation supporting justification, wrapping, and highlights |\n| `Syntax` | `rich/syntax.py` | Lexes and styles source code across languages using Pygments lexers |\n| `Traceback` | `rich/traceback.py` | Exception traceback visualizer highlighting code context and local variables |\n| `Tree` | `rich/tree.py` | Recursive tree diagram builder with customizable guide lines |\n| `Theme` | `rich/theme.py` | Container mapping semantic style names to `Style` instances |\n| `TerminalTheme` | `rich/terminal_theme.py` | Terminal color scheme definitions (ANSI 16 colors + background + foreground) |\n\n## Testing & Verification\n- Test commands: `pytest tests/test_table.py tests/test_text.py tests/test_syntax.py tests/test_traceback.py tests/test_tree.py`\n- Test files: `tests/test_table.py`, `tests/test_text.py`, `tests/test_syntax.py`, `tests/test_traceback.py`, `tests/test_tree.py`\n\n## Non-obvious Details\n- **Table Width Solving in `rich/table.py` (L523–L585, ADR-0004)**:\n  - `Table._calculate_column_widths(self, console: Console, options: ConsoleOptions) -> List[int]` (L523): Computes column widths (including padding, excluding border `self._extra_width`).\n  - When `self.expand` is True and `columns` have `flexible` ratios (L535–L555), `flex_minimum` (L543) computes minimum widths for flexible columns (`max((column.min_width or 1) + get_padding_width(column._index), _range.minimum)`), and distributes `flexible_width = max(sum(flex_minimum), max_width - sum(fixed_widths))` via `ratio_distribute(flexible_width, ratios, flex_minimum)`.\n  - When `table_width > max_width` (L556–L575), `_collapse_widths` and `ratio_reduce` shrink columns, but must enforce `min_widths = [(column.min_width or 1) + get_padding_width(column._index) for column in columns]` so flexible columns never collapse to 0 width (`max_reduce = [max(0, w - min_w) for w, min_w in zip(widths, min_widths)]` and `widths = [max(min_w, _range.maximum or 0) ...]`).\n- **Traceback suppression flags**: Setting `_rich_traceback_omit = True` or `_rich_traceback_guard = True` inside a function's local scope conceals internal boilerplate frames during crashes.\n- **Text span arithmetic**: When slicing or joining `Text` objects, character index spans are adjusted or split automatically to preserve original formatting.\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n- **Table row modification during iteration**: Adding rows to a `Table` while rendering it concurrently will trigger size calculation mismatches.\n- **Traceback hook installation in libraries**: Calling `rich.traceback.install()` inside library code replaces global `sys.excepthook`, which can interfere with host application exception handling.\n\n\n## Related KIs\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/align.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/ansi.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/cells.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/columns.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/console.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/constrain.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/containers.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/control.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]] (via `rich/default_styles.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]] (via `rich/highlighter.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]] (via `rich/jupyter.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/__init__.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/color.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/color_triplet.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/emoji.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]] (via `rich/_loop.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]] (via `rich/markdown.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]] (via `rich/markup.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]] (via `rich/measure.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]] (via `rich/padding.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]] (via `rich/palette.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]] (via `rich/panel.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]] (via `rich/protocol.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]] (via `rich/_pick.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]] (via `rich/_ratio.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]] (via `rich/_timer.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]] (via `rich/_wrap.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]] (via `rich/scope.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]] (via `rich/segment.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]] (via `rich/style.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]] (via `rich/styled.py`)\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":61,"timestamp":1794170343354},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_Qef9synB0c48qJcjhfvVFkya","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0003: Style Composition & ANSI Sequences\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nStyling in terminals requires combining foreground colors, background colors, links, and various text attributes (bold, italic, underline, reverse, etc.). Rich needs an immutable, high-performance styling algebra that supports cascading inheritance, markup parsing, and export to both ANSI terminals and web formats (HTML/SVG).\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Immutable Style Class:**  \n   The `Style` object is immutable and hashable with internal caching:\n   - Attributes (bold, underline, double_underline, italic, blink, etc.) use tri-state values (`True`, `False`, `None` where `None` indicates inherit/unset).\n2. **Style Composition Algebra (`+` operator):**  \n   Style addition (`style1 + style2`) cascades attributes from left to right:\n   - Attributes defined in `style2` override attributes in `style1` if set (`is not None`).\n   - Unset attributes (`None`) in `style2` inherit values from `style1`.\n3. **ANSI Sequence Mapping & Exporters:**  \n   Every new style modifier must maintain synchronization across:\n   - Terminal ANSI code generator: open code (e.g. `\\x1b[4:2m` or `\\x1b[21m`) and reset/close code.\n   - Default style definitions (`rich/default_styles.py`).\n   - Markup parser (`rich/markup.py`) to recognize `[modifier]...[/]`.\n   - Exporters (`rich/terminal_theme.py`, `rich/_export_format.py`) for SVG and HTML rendering.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Full consistency between CLI console output, HTML export, and SVG snapshots.\n- Guarantees predictable cascading style resolution across nested tags.\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":72,"timestamp":1794170343365},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Inspecting code patterns**\n\nI need to take a close look at the code patterns, specifically focusing on initialization, measurement, and perhaps styling in a straightforward manner. It’s important to make sure I’m catching any details that could help improve clarity and functionality. I wonder if keeping it simple will also enhance readability. Let’s consider the best approach to make the code as effective as possible while ensuring it remains easy to understand!","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.summary\",\"summary\":\"**Inspecting code patterns**\\n\\nI need to take a close look at the code patterns, specifically focusing on initialization, measurement, and perhaps styling in a straightforward manner. It’s important to make sure I’m catching any details that could help improve clarity and functionality. I